OpenAMRobot Platform Firmware

This repository is part of the OpenAMRobot open-source robotics ecosystem.

Project:
OpenAMRobot - Affordable Open Autonomous Mobile Robot Platform

Organization:
https://github.com/openAMRobot

Website:
https://botshare.ai

Purpose:
This repository contains the low-level motor-control firmware, documentation,
and configuration for the Teensy 4.0 that drives the OpenAMRobot base
(micro-ROS motor control, encoder odometry, IMU integration, and the
/debug telemetry contract).

Important notice:
This firmware drives real motors on a physical robot. Users are responsible
for validating safety, wiring, and mechanical limits before flashing or
running it on hardware. The software is provided for educational, research,
prototyping, and development purposes.

